cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. This is a
  software citation: no paper describing MOTAR has been published, so there is
  no preferred-citation entry. Add one here when a paper exists.
title: "MOTAR: measured perception error and safety-filter diagnosis for UAV interception in simulation"
abstract: >-
  A simulation-only research repository studying UAV interception under learned
  perception. It measures when and why a direction-preserving speed filter
  fails, trains a detector on real air-to-air video and injects its measured
  error into the simulator, and measures how well a target's apparent size
  recovers metric range on public footage with survey-grade ground truth. No
  real-flight result is claimed.
type: software
authors:
  # The repository records a GitHub handle and an email for its author and
  # nothing more. A legal name and an ORCID are NOT recorded anywhere in this
  # repository, so they are deliberately left out rather than guessed; add them
  # here when you want them in the citation. Verified from `git log` and the
  # origin remote, both of which agree.
  - name: "joshualikaist"
    email: "kaist.mesc@gmail.com"
    website: "https://github.com/joshualikaist"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshualikaist/MOTAR"
url: "https://github.com/joshualikaist/MOTAR"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - simulation
  - perception
  - safety filter
  - reproducibility
date-released: "2026-09-12"
references:
